  "_source": "A real, complete 'Art and Design Form 1 Scheme of Work, Term 1-3' (a real Zambian secondary school; the source's own teacher name and school name are not reproduced here per this app's standing sourcing policy) was shared with this project and reviewed in full. This replaces this file's earlier content, which was pieced together from two separate, individually incomplete CDC teaching-module extracts (one starting mid-sequence at topic 1.11, the other beginning mid-sequence at 1.2.3, both missing real topics entirely) -- this new source covers Form 1 topics 1.1-1.14 across all three terms without gaps, and cites real page numbers from the official '2024 Art and Design Syllabus, Ordinary Secondary Education Form 1-4' throughout (e.g. 'pg. 2', 'pg. 12'), confirming its own topic and outcome numbering tracks that official syllabus directly. Topic, sub-topic and Specific Competence statements are the source's own real wording; its own Content/Concept and Learning Activities columns are omitted, consistent with the approach used for every other bundled subject in this app. Term placement for every topic is real, read directly from which Term block of the source document it appears in. A few sub-topics in the source had their own numbering visibly collide across adjacent weeks (e.g. two different sub-topics both initially labelled '2.2.1' for Colour Properties and Colour Pigments) -- resolved here by keeping the source's own topic-level number and renumbering only the colliding sub-topic sequence, without altering any competency wording.",
